# Documented, dated exemptions for the `container` workflow's image
# vulnerability scan (`.github/workflows/container.yml`) — mirrors the
# same "documented, dated exemption" convention `.github/workflows/
# deps.yml`'s own pip-audit `--ignore-vuln` flags already use, rather
# than a silent, undated suppression.
#
# Both entries below are OS-package advisories in the `python:3.12-slim`
# base image (Debian's `libssl3t64`/`openssl`), not anything this
# repository's own code or dependencies introduce. No patched Debian
# package is resolvable through the currently-published `python:3.12-
# slim` tag yet. Revisit and remove once Debian ships the fix and a
# fresh `docker build` no longer reports it — do not carry either of
# these past that point.
#
# Added 2026-09-30.

# CVE-2026-75804 — openssl: OpenSSL Denial of Service via unenforced
# QUIC connection flow control. Fixed in 3.5.7-1~deb13u3; the currently
# resolvable python:3.12-slim image carries 3.5.7-1~deb13u2.
CVE-2026-75804

# CVE-2026-84782 — openssl: compat-openssl: Information disclosure via
# DTLS handshake retransmission. Same fixed/installed version gap as
# CVE-2026-75804 above.
CVE-2026-84782
